---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="LitSquare Skills — Skills for work"
  description="Add portable AI Skills once, organize them into Kits, and use them with the assistants you already know."
>
  <section class="hero page-shell">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span></span> Native macOS app · In development</div>
    <h1>Skills for work, in the AI tools your team already uses.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Add a Skill once. Organize related Skills into Kits. LitSquare Skills keeps one
      understandable local library and handles the technical details quietly.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/directory/">Explore the directory</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/thierryc/litsquare-skills-directory/issues/new/choose">Follow the project</a>
    </div>
    <div class="window" aria-label="Concept preview of the LitSquare Skills library">
      <div class="window-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>LitSquare Skills</span></div>
      <div class="window-body">
        <aside>
          <strong>Library</strong>
          <a class="selected">⌂ <span>Home</span></a>
          <a>◇ <span>Skills</span></a>
          <a>⌕ <span>Discover</span></a>
        </aside>
        <div class="preview-content">
          <div class="preview-heading"><div><small>YOUR KITS</small><h2>Ready when you are</h2></div><button>Add</button></div>
          <div class="kit-row"><span class="kit-icon violet">D</span><div><strong>Design Critique</strong><small>2 Skills · Valid</small></div><b>›</b></div>
          <div class="kit-row"><span class="kit-icon coral">B</span><div><strong>Brand Deep Dive</strong><small>3 Skills · Available soon</small></div><b>›</b></div>
          <div class="health"><span>✓</span><div><strong>Your local library is healthy</strong><small>No files are duplicated between assistants.</small></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="steps page-shell" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <p class="section-label">A calmer way to work</p>
    <h2 id="how-heading">Three ideas, no terminal required.</h2>
    <div class="step-grid">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Add once</h3><p>Review what a Skill contains, where it came from, and what it may need before adding it.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Build a Kit</h3><p>Group useful Skills around the work—not around hidden folders or a particular vendor.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Stay in control</h3><p>Local edits are protected. Changes are staged, auditable, recoverable, and written in human language.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="audience-band">
    <div class="page-shell audience-grid">
      <div><p class="section-label">Designed for real teams</p><h2>Start with the work, not the machinery.</h2></div>
      <div class="pills" aria-label="Initial audiences"><span>Brand</span><span>Product design</span><span>Research</span><span>Content</span><span>Marketing</span><span>Design operations</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="principles page-shell">
    <div class="principle-main">
      <p class="section-label">Local by default</p>
      <h2>Your library stays understandable and portable.</h2>
      <p>LitSquare Skills uses ordinary folders and Markdown, requires no LitSquare account, and does not execute scripts packaged with a Skill.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/standards/">Read the interoperability approach →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="principle-list">
      <div><strong>One source of truth</strong><span>Store each Skill once.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Review before change</strong><span>Installation is never discovery.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Practical undo</strong><span>Backups and audit history are built in.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Open formats</strong><span>Agent Skills stays intact.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing page-shell">
    <p class="section-label">Building in public</p>
    <h2>The local library comes first.</h2>
    <p>The directory is open for schemas, documentation, and feedback while the native app completes its safety foundation.</p>
    <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/thierryc/litsquare-skills-directory">View the public repository</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
